# Environment Variables

This file documents all environment variables used by the application.
**Never commit real values to source control.**

## Required

| Variable | Description |
|---|---|
| `NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL` | Your Supabase project URL (e.g. `https://xxxx.supabase.co`) |
| `NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY` | Your Supabase anon/public key |

## Optional

| Variable | Default | Description |
|---|---|---|
| `NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL` | `https://morrow.market` | Canonical site URL for metadata |

## Setup

1. Copy this file: `cp .env.example .env.local`
2. Fill in your Supabase values from the [Supabase Dashboard](https://app.supabase.com)
3. `.env.local` is gitignored and will never be committed

## Security Rules

- Variables prefixed with `NEXT_PUBLIC_` are bundled into the browser build — never put secrets there.
- Server-only secrets (future: service role key) must NOT have the `NEXT_PUBLIC_` prefix.
- Validation happens at startup in `lib/env.ts` — missing required variables throw immediately.
